        "created_at": "2014-12-15T18:43:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"xThe Killswitch\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n xThe Killswitch:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Pydro wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Afterall, you wouldn't want Darken the Sky to play every card in Matty's deck.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThis right here makes the most sense for me, and I better understand the distinction.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Wouldn't make any difference (specifically for Darken the Skies) if the cards were put into play or played in The Matriarch's case*, she specifies \"from the villain deck\" so it wouldn't trigger either way.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>*I'm not using Matty, some of us don't want to be \"<em>lucky\"</em><em>&nbsp;</em></p>",
