        "created_at": "2014-12-15T20:55:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>SImilarly, \"players cannot play cards\" is not the same as \"hero cards cannot be played.\" As per Paul in some super old thread or another, an effect that plays the top card of the deck (like Setback, or the Atlantis Fountain, whatever it's called; not the pillars of Hercules, the other one) is TECHNICALLY not the PLAYER playing the card, so it can get around \"players cannot play cards,\" but not \"hero cards cannot be played.\"</p>",
